# Valgrind suppressions for TestFileServer alone, besides poc-gc.supp.
#
# The collector scans each task's stack conservatively, as it does the
# main stack (poc-gc.supp): every word goes to MarkCandidate, written or
# not. A word never written in a frame of SocketTasks.Await or of the
# test's Whole can still hold a stale pointer into a live block, which
# MarkCandidate then marks and pushes; DrainMarkStack, tracing that
# block, uses the address derived from the unwritten word, and memcheck
# reports it there: 22 "Use of uninitialised value of size 8", the
# same on every run, each "created by a stack allocation" in one of
# those two procedures (--track-origins, 2026-11-18). That is the
# conservative scan, not posockets.
#
# It is kept out of poc-gc.supp, which every test uses, because the same
# report also comes from a record copied whole into the heap, carrying
# its uninitialised padding, which is the program's to fix (pogeminilib's
# PLAN.md, Phase 2).
{
   poc-gc-drainmarkstack-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.DrainMarkStack
}
